### `e1684`: ECOG melanoma trial E1684

`e1684` comes from the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group trial E1684 of high-dose interferon
alfa-2b as adjuvant therapy for melanoma, in 284 patients. Many patients never relapse, so the
Kaplan-Meier curve levels off well above zero. That plateau is the signature of a cured fraction,
and it makes `e1684` the standard dataset for cure models.

**Columns:** `TRT` (`0` = control, `1` = interferon), `FAILTIME` (relapse-free time in years),
`FAILCENS` (`0` = censored, `1` = relapse), `AGE` (age centered at its mean), `SEX` (`0` = male,
`1` = female).

**Model fit:** `e1684` is designed for `MixtureCure`, which models who is cured (the incidence
submodel) separately from when the uncured relapse (the latency submodel). The response is
`Surv(FAILTIME, FAILCENS)`. The [mixture cure section](parametric-models.qmd#mixture-cure-models)
of the parametric models page uses it throughout. It also works for Kaplan-Meier curves and
log-rank tests comparing the two arms.

